In LaTeX, `\rowcolor` is used to color an entire row of a table. It comes from the `xcolor` package with the `table` option.

```latex
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}
```

Example:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}

\begin{document}

\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
\hline
\rowcolor{gray!30}
A & B & C \\
\hline
1 & 2 & 3 \\
\rowcolor{yellow}
4 & 5 & 6 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}

\end{document}
```

You can also use custom colors:

```latex
\definecolor{myblue}{RGB}{220,230,255}

\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
\rowcolor{myblue}
Name & Score \\
\hline
Alice & 95 \\
Bob & 88 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
```

For alternating row colors, use `\rowcolors`:

```latex
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}

\rowcolors{2}{gray!15}{white}

\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
Name & Score \\
\hline
Alice & 95 \\
Bob & 88 \\
Charlie & 91 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
```

Here, rows starting from row 2 alternate between `gray!15` and `white`.

